<DocLayout title="Components" description="Farn component patterns — layout, navigation, actions, forms, data display, and status feedback">
  <h1>Components</h1>
  <p>
    Farn is a design token system with an optional component layer. Tokens give you the
    vocabulary; component classes give you a starting point — override the tokens to retheme
    without touching the classes.
  </p>
  <p>All component classes consume semantic tokens so they adapt to dark/light mode and surface context automatically.</p>

  <h2>Layout</h2>
  <p>Structural components for organising content. Cards surface discrete items in scannable grids; section transitions create intentional visual breaks between full-width areas. See <a href="/components/layout">Layout</a> for live demos and full CSS reference.</p>

  <h2>Navigation</h2>
  <p>Components that help users orient and move through a site. Breadcrumbs show position in a hierarchy; accordions reveal content progressively without leaving the page. See <a href="/components/navigation">Navigation</a>.</p>

  <h2>Actions</h2>
  <p>Components that trigger operations or navigate users. Four button variants cover the full intent spectrum; <code>--btn-*</code> Tier-3 tokens let the entire button palette be rethemed in one place. Inline links use <code>--link-*</code> tokens independently of <code>--color-accent</code>. See <a href="/components/actions">Actions</a>.</p>

  <h2>Forms</h2>
  <p>Form element styles ship as bare element selectors — no extra classes required on <code>input</code>, <code>textarea</code>, or <code>select</code>. All styles consume <code>--input-*</code> Tier-3 tokens. See <a href="/components/forms">Forms</a>.</p>

  <h2>Data</h2>
  <p>Components for labelling and presenting structured information. Seven badge variants use opaque palette fills so they read on any surface without dark-mode overrides. See <a href="/components/data">Data</a>.</p>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <p>Feedback components for async state and high-priority interruptions. Alerts, loading states, and modal dialogs are planned — state tokens for errors, warnings, and success already exist in the token system. See <a href="/components/status">Status</a>.</p>

  <h3>Loading components</h3>
  <p>All component classes ship in <code>dist/farn-components.css</code>. Load it alongside <code>farn.css</code> or <code>farn-tokens.css</code>.</p>
  <pre><code>&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/farn-theme/dist/farn.css"&gt;
&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/farn-theme/dist/farn-components.css"&gt;</code></pre>

  <h3>Surfaces and theme context</h3>
  <p>All components inherit the correct tokens automatically when placed inside a <code>data-surface</code> or <code>data-theme</code> context.</p>
  <pre><code>&lt;!-- depth levels (relative to page theme) --&gt;
&lt;section data-surface="base"&gt; … &lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section data-surface="layer"&gt; … &lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section data-surface="overlay"&gt; … &lt;/section&gt;

&lt;!-- forced theme (sets background + all tokens) --&gt;
&lt;section data-theme="dark"&gt; … &lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section data-theme="dark" data-surface="layer"&gt; … &lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
</DocLayout>
